From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:49:57 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 94/99] Reserved shortcuts never reach the page, however AppKit
 delivers them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A page focused in the key window (a Google Sheets grid) could still get
⌘⌥↑/↓ first and keep it: the browser now checks every key it is about to
hand to a page against the reserved shortcuts, by the key's Mac key code
and modifiers (what reaches a page may lack the characters the menus
match by), and runs the command instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
